  2| //! (issue #1113, the G11 half).
  3| //!
  4| //! Until now the only thing persisting agent memory was the automatic
  5| //! [`memory_loop`](super::memory_loop) — retrieve → inject → store around every
  6| //! turn, unsteerable from inside the turn. These three tools add the
  7| //! deliberate half: an agent that just learned the customer's fiscal year can
  8| //! *choose* to keep it, find it again next week, and discard it when it stops
  9| //! being true.
 10| //!
 11| //! # Why these are oc-authored rather than the vendored upstream tools
 12| //!
 13| //! Upstream's `MemoryStoreTool` / `MemoryRecallTool` resolve their store
 14| //! through an ambient `CoreContext` (or a process-global fallback) that this
 15| //! crate's multi-tenant-in-one-process model never scopes — wiring them would
 16| //! be a cross-company memory leak, which is exactly why `build.rs` withheld
 17| //! them (see `memory_tools`'s history there). These implementations follow the
 18| //! `workspace_tools` pattern instead: the company and agent are **fields
 19| //! captured at build time**, the port is the company's own [`ContextStore`],
 20| //! and `execute()` has no ambient anything to reach. Upstream's schemas also
 21| //! take `namespace` as a model-supplied parameter — handing the model the
 22| //! tenant boundary as a free-text field. Here the namespace is derived from
 23| //! the captured identity, always.
 24| //!
 25| //! # Where the memories live
 26| //!
 27| //! `ContextStore` rows labelled `agent-memory/<agent id>/<slug>` — the same
 28| //! store and label family the automatic loop and the Brain console already
 29| //! read, so a deliberate memory surfaces in ambient recall and in the
 30| //! operator's Brain view like any other context row, and travels with the
 31| //! export bundle. Writes are `Internal` taint by authorship (the agent's own
 32| //! conclusion — same precedent as operator facts), which is why they go
 33| //! through `deps.context`, not the inbound port.
 34| //!
 35| //! # What forget may touch
 36| //!
 37| //! Only rows under this agent's own `agent-memory/<agent id>/` prefix. Recall
 38| //! surfaces everything — task outcomes, operator-fact mirrors, other agents'
 39| //! memories — but delete is scoped to what this agent deliberately stored:
 40| //! task outcomes are the loop's record, and operator facts are the operator's.
 41| //! The guard is a list-membership check against the agent's own prefix, and
 42| //! the delete itself is **label-scoped** (`ContextStore::delete_label`, issue
 43| //! #1300): it removes exactly this agent's own claims, so a hallucinated or
 44| //! copied address cannot reach anyone else's rows even when byte-identical
 45| //! content put their label on the same content address — the other labels
 46| //! keep the body, which is reaped only with its last claim.
